{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"code":"Nexus()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"The archetype storage","anchor":"The-archetype-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the numbers say","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Case","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2.5 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.4 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"3.6 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"227 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 200 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1 800 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a family, 2 components","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"455 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"455 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Random ","type":"text"},{"code":"entity.get","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"334 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"345 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4 900 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1 730 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 510 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","alignments":["left","right","right"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two (","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Which storage to pick","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Differences you can observe","anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the spans.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"topic","kind":"section","title":"What the numbers say","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"title":"NexusEvent","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"topic","title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"archetype","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/SavingAndLoadingScenes":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store a whole "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" on disk and load it again with the same entities, components and entity identifiers."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/savingandloadingscenes","title":"Saving and Loading Scenes","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sparseSet"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type, a bitset per entity."}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Family/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)":{"title":"forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/family\/foreachcomponentspan(reading:writing:_:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"each C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"forEachComponentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","text":"Span","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV","text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterates the members of this family in batches, giving "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the components of a batch as contiguous spans."}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","type":"topic","title":"clear()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ComponentMacro":{"title":"Generating components with the component macro","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties.","type":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"topic","kind":"section","title":"Which storage to pick","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#Which-storage-to-pick"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"flecs"}],"title":"flecs","url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to."}],"title":"NexusEventMask","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"code":"Span","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"}